.TH PM_PROBE 1 "May 2026" "v1.9.10a" "CamClops - Camera Profiler"
.SH NAME
clops_probe \- camera compatibility profiler for the CamClops suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clops_probe
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I file.ts
.PP
.B clops_probe
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I MID\fR:\fITID
.PP
.B clops_probe
.B \-\-card
.I PATH
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
.B clops_probe
.B \-\-wizard
.I PATH
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clops_probe
inspects dashcam footage files and reports video characteristics,
stream layout, and GPS metadata format.  It is primarily intended to
help users determine whether an unsupported camera model is compatible
with CamClops, and to collect the information needed to request support
for a new camera via a GitHub issue.
.PP
Cameras confirmed working with the current profile system:
.BR "Pruveeo D90" " (MPEG-TS, LIGO GPS stream, 4-channel subdirectory layout),"
.BR "Cobra CCDC4500" " (MOV/3GP, no GPS, single-channel flat layout),"
.BR "Cobra GPS" " (MOV/3GP, GPS0 atom, 2-channel flat layout),"
.BR "Prilotte" " (AVI/MJPEG, no GPS, mtime timestamps, 2-channel subdirectory layout)."
Other cameras may work with a custom profile built by the wizard.
.PP
Single-file and
.I MID:TID
modes probe one segment and print a concise report.
.PP
Card mode
.RB ( \-\-card )
walks an entire dashcam storage root, identifies camera subdirectories,
samples segment durations, and probes the first segment of the primary
camera directory.  The report is formatted to be pasted directly into
a GitHub issue.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I file.ts
Probe a single footage segment.  The path must be absolute or resolvable
from the current directory.
.TP
.I MID\fR:\fITID
Probe the first Front camera segment of a known trip identified by its
manifest ID and trip ID.  Uses the CamClops manifest index to resolve the
segment path.
.TP
.B \-\-card \fIPATH
Fingerprint a dashcam storage root.
.I PATH
should be the top-level directory that contains the camera subdirectories
.RB ( Front/ ,
.BR Rear/ ,
etc.).  Candidate camera directories are identified as any first-level
subdirectory of
.I PATH
that contains video files.  If no subdirectories contain video files but
.I PATH
itself does, the root is treated as a flat single-directory layout and
camera identity is inferred from filename tokens.  Supported token styles
include bare single-letter suffix
.RB ( F ,
.BR R ,
.BR L ,
.BR B ),
underscore-prefixed letter
.RB ( _F ,
.BR _R ),
multi-part embedded tokens
.RB ( _CAM1_VID ,
.BR _CAM2_VID ),
and prefix tokens where the camera identifier precedes the timestamp.
Hidden files and macOS resource forks (names beginning with
.BR . )
are ignored during all scans.
Up to five segments are sampled for duration measurements; the full probe
is performed on the first segment of the primary camera directory.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON output instead of the default text report.  Suitable for
automated processing.
.TP
.B \-\-wizard \fIPATH
Interactive camera profile builder.  Walks the dashcam storage root at
.I PATH
and guides the user through:
.RS
.IP \(bu 3
Camera role assignment (Front/Rear/Left/Right) — from subdirectory names
for cameras that use a directory per channel, or from filename tokens
for cameras that store all channels in one directory.  A two-pane
interface shows the standard slot names on the left and the detected
source paths with sample filenames on the right; press
.BR F / R / L / B
to select a slot then a source number to assign it.
.IP \(bu 3
Filename timestamp format and timestamp timezone
.RB ( local
or
.BR utc ).
.IP \(bu 3
Thumbnail handling — sidecar
.I _ths.jpg
files detected automatically;
falls back to generate-on-demand via ffmpeg if not found.
.IP \(bu 3
GPS method and cold-start lock offset.
.IP \(bu 3
Profile name.
.RE
.PP
On completion the profile is saved in CameraProfile JSON format to
.I ~/.config/camclops/profiles/<name>.json
and a trial scan is run immediately to confirm that the saved profile
detects trips correctly.
.TP
.B \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the CamClops version string and exit.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
.SS Text — single-file mode
.nf
File:         /z/srcdash/ex2/Front/20260209_043838F.ts
Container:    MPEG-TS (.ts)
Resolution:   1920x1080
Frame rate:   25 fps
Pixel format: yuvj420p  (full-range)
Color space:  bt709
Duration:     180s
Streams:      video(0) audio(1) data(2)
GPS method:   LIGOGPSINFO (stream 2)
GPS first fix: 2026:02:09 10:39:14  lat=30.419000  lon=-89.025191
.fi
.SS Text \(em card mode
.nf
--- clops_probe SD Card Fingerprint ---
Root:         /media/sdcard
Camera dirs:  Front/ Rear/ Left/ Right/
Extensions:   .jpg .ts
Filename pattern (sample):
  Front/20260209_043838F.ts
  Front/20260209_044140F.ts
Segment lengths observed: 180s 180s 180s (stub at end noted if present)
Video profile (Front, first segment):
  Resolution:   1920x1080
  Frame rate:   25 fps
  Pixel format: yuvj420p (full-range)
  Color space:  bt709
Timestamp:    filename (YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS)
GPS method:   LIGOGPSINFO  -- GPS in private LIGO stream
GPS first fix: 2026:02:09 10:39:14  lat=30.419000  lon=-89.025191

--- Submit this report to: https://github.com/Nutball-Labs/CamClops/issues ---
.fi
.SH "GPS METHOD VALUES"
.TP
.B LIGOGPSINFO
The file contains a private binary data stream tagged
.B LIGO
in the container.  This is the format used by Pruveeo D90 footage.
ExifTool must support the LIGOGPSINFO stream format for extraction to work.
If GPS extraction fails for your camera, contact the ExifTool maintainer
directly.  See
.BR exiftool (1).
.TP
.B Standard GPS metadata
GPS metadata was successfully extracted by ExifTool using the configured
extraction options, but no
.B LIGO
private data stream was detected.  The camera uses a standard or
otherwise identifiable GPS metadata format.
.TP
.B Not detected
No GPS data was found.  Either the camera does not record GPS, the footage
was recorded without a GPS fix, or the configured ExifTool options are
incompatible with the camera's GPS format.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Probe a single file:
.B clops_probe /mnt/sdcard/Front/20260209_043838F.ts
.TP
Probe a trip's first segment via MID:TID:
.B clops_probe X1:87
.TP
Fingerprint an entire SD card:
.B clops_probe \-\-card /mnt/sdcard
.TP
Machine-readable card fingerprint for a GitHub issue:
.B clops_probe \-\-card /mnt/sdcard \-\-json
.TP
Create a camera profile interactively and verify with a trial scan:
.B clops_probe \-\-wizard /mnt/sdcard
.SH "REQUESTING CAMERA SUPPORT"
If your dashcam is not supported, first try the wizard:
.PP
.RS
.B clops_probe \-\-wizard \fIPATH
.RE
.PP
If the wizard does not produce a working profile, collect a fingerprint
and open a GitHub issue:
.PP
.RS
.B clops_probe \-\-card \fIPATH\fB \-\-json > camera_report.json
.RE
.PP
Open a GitHub issue at
.B https://github.com/Nutball-Labs/CamClops/issues
and attach
.IR camera_report.json .
Include the camera make and model in the issue title.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/camclops/manifests.json
Manifest index — used only when resolving
.I MID:TID
arguments.
.TP
.I ~/.config/camclops/profiles/<name>.json
Camera profile written by
.BR \-\-wizard .
Loaded by
.B camclops
when the active profile ID matches
.IR <name> .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Probe completed successfully (GPS may or may not have been found).
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, file not found, or
.I MID:TID
not in the manifest index.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR camclops (1),
.BR clops_gpsinfo (1),
.BR clops_gpsexport (1),
.BR ffprobe (1),
.BR exiftool (1)
